{
  "_comment": [
    "The sign-in page's notice on a live medium: gxwi-config's line, and how",
    "to sign in there, as the medium's peios account, which has no password.",
    "",
    "For a live medium only. An image lists it in [registry] live_autoapply,",
    "which applies after the base queue, so this Notice is the one a medium",
    "shows, and which installerd never copies to the disk it installs: an",
    "installed machine shows gxwi-config's alone, and has no peios account.",
    "",
    "Shipped by dev.peios.gxwi as a regim master."
  ],
  "keys": [
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Software",
      "values": []
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Software\\GXWI",
      "values": []
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Software\\GXWI\\Logon",
      "values": [
        {
          "name": "Notice",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": [
            "Development image. GXWI is served over HTTPS with a certificate this machine made for itself, so your browser warns before you first sign in. Before you go on, check that the SHA-256 fingerprint your browser shows for it matches this machine's: sign in at its console as peios and run cat /var/state/gxwi/certificate.sha256.",
            "The live image account is peios, with no password."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
